# Cursor & Kiro Agent Rules for Capability Hub AI

- Always inspect `AGENTS.md` and `.kiro/instructions.md` before making architectural modifications. `AGENTS.md` is the source of truth.
- The live backend is Python/FastAPI in `backend/app/`. Backend changes go there. `server.ts` / `server-db.ts` is frozen except to keep the Google AI Studio deployment working.
- Keep all Gemini API calls server-side — `backend/app/ai.py` (`google-genai`, model `gemini-3.6-flash`). Never expose `GEMINI_API_KEY` to the browser.
- Verify frontend changes with `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`) and `npm run build`.
- Verify backend changes with `python backend/scripts/verify_authz_scenarios.py http://localhost:8000` — it must stay 46/46.
- Maintain the dark enterprise theme palette (#141E30 canvas, #0F1724 cards, #4F8EF7 / #10B981 accents).
- Do not remove hardware permission declarations (`camera`, `microphone`) from `metadata.json`.
